      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e9a140/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-01-23T02:59:45.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Looking around at the guides for heroes and promo-versions of heroes, it seems the consensus is that standard Ra (with base power that damages) is generally better than the Ra: Horus promo (who trades damage for a card drawing base power).&nbsp; So I was a bit surprised by the statistics report, that shows Ra: Horus being about 4% more effective, and getting incapacitated 1% less often when compared to standard Ra.</p><p>Any ideas on why?&nbsp; Is it that Ra: Horus's card drawing leads to more combos, and that this is generally a more effective tactic?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:03.913Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
