    {
      "id": 87481,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-01-23T14:50:03.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"squad\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e9a140/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> squad:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So I was a bit surprised by the statistics report, that shows Ra: Horus being about 4% more effective, and getting incapacitated 1% less often when compared to standard Ra. Any ideas on why?&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>About the statistics. Because the data pool is still very low and varied between the two Ras, you should really take those numbers with a grain of salt big enough to choke a donkey.</p>\n<p>Beard Ra is going to mill through his deck much quicker than base Ra. This likely means a quicker Imbued Fire. Seeing IF faster on average could certainly have an effect on overall win %. Beard Ra players are also more likely to play into the \"Staffarang\" style of play contributing to less incaps.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:11:46.720Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
