      "id": 87486,
      "name": "Oaktree",
      "username": "Oaktree",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/oaktree/{size}/2287_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-01-24T02:26:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Probably have to look further into the situational stats since Ra and Ra-Horus are different enough in style that things will make a difference.</p><p>I got handed a random game tonight that was Ra-Horus, Eternal Haka, and AZ vs Advanced Kismet in The Final Wasteland.&nbsp; I normally consider Kismet a relatively weak villain, though somewhat more tolerable on advanced since with some draws she can get kookily dangerous.</p><p>I got my head handed to me.&nbsp; Yes, Ra-Horus got cards out and started putting together a nice damage engine; just in time for Inconcevible Obstruction and Lady Luck to come out and spike it.&nbsp; Along with Eternal Haka getting pulverized due to jinx cards.&nbsp; Ra went down last since he was cycling Staff of Ra at one point to heal points.&nbsp; AZ did little since the initial draw was minor cards and two copies of his trash-picking card.</p><p>(I consider that group a fairly weak 3-hero team.&nbsp; Very little on-going removal.&nbsp; And with Haka and Ra in \"draw card\" version compared to \"damage out the gate\" I couldn't dish damage out early or consistent enough since all three were sort of long-run heroes.)</p>",
      "post_number": 12,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:11:47.119Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
